Fair spin lock: Ticket locks on x86 implemented using locked add limit throughput by disallowing threads from gaining lock until they hold the ticket. Modified this to do range based ticket locking in which all ticket owners within a certain range can claim lock.

Greedy Cache Efficient Spinlock (distributed spinlock) Implemented a spinlock where groups of threads spin on node locks and global queue does arbitration between separate node locks. When local node lock has no further contenders instead of releasing lock back to global queue this implementation keeps it there and lets other nodes steal it lazily using proxy threads. Reduces cacheline traffic substantially.

